## Cursor Rules

- Service shared contracts must live in `I<ServiceName>.ts`.
- Repository/domain contracts must live in `<Domain>Model.ts`.
- Reusable domain constant sets must use shared enums instead of repeated string literals.
- No inline `interface`/`type` declarations inside service or processor implementation files.
- Public service/repository methods must have explicit return types.
- Keep services/repositories lean and responsibility-focused.
- Use descriptive camelCase variable names (`txClient`, `badgeDefinition`, `eventContext`) and avoid ambiguous short names (`tx`, `def`, `ctx`, `res`) for domain logic.
- Constructor-injected dependency fields must use descriptive type-aligned names (`deduplicationService`, `configService`, `usersRepository`) and must not use shortened aliases like `dedup`, `config`, or `repo`.
- Use one top-level try/catch per public service method.
- Avoid nested try/catch blocks in the same method.
- For cache pass-through paths, use graceful fallback (`.catch` + warn) instead of dedicated try/catch.
- Log structured context on errors and throw safe Nest exceptions for HTTP consumers.
- Do not change `2xx` response body shapes unless explicitly requested.
